<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Jefferson-Pilot raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Jefferson-Pilot raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch analyst Edward Spehar said he upgraded his near-term rating on Jefferson-Pilot Corp to buy from accumulate, keeping a long-term buy rating on the stock.</p>
<p>-- Jefferson-Pilot named a Focus One stock at Merrill.</p>
<p>-- stock was up 2-11/16 to 71-3/4.  </p>
<p>-- In a report, Spehar said that, following a strong second quarter raised 1997 operating earnings estimate to $4.25 from $4.10 and 1998 view to $5.10 from $4.85.</p>
<p>-- said company is delivering rapid and accelerating EPS growth, plus an improving return on equity, a rarity in the insurance industry.</p>
</text>
